{
  "description": "Speaker-background layer wire contract, KRI-1558 extension (`layout_windows`, capability `speakerSections`, protocol 54): how the speaker is drawn in each span of the edit. `own` = her own take, full-frame and untouched (as inside a full-screen window); `full` = the cut-out speaker at full size over the picture; `small` = the cut-out speaker at `frame` (a `speaker_frame`, same bounds) over the picture; `picture` = the picture alone, the speaker not drawn (her voice plays on). Output seconds, `start <= t < end`; each window lasts at least 0.5 s, starts at 0 or later and ends within 1800 s; sorted by `start`, never overlapping (touching ends are fine), 1...40 of them. `frame` is present exactly when `layout` is `small` (`frame: null` elsewhere reads as absent). Per frame a full-screen window wins over a layout window, and a layout window replaces the layer's `speaker_frame`. Every `valid` layer must decode (Python SpeakerBackgroundLayer, Swift SpeakerBackgroundLayer), equal its `normalized` form and re-encode to it; every `invalid` entry must be rejected by both. v1.json to v5.json still apply unchanged: a layer without the key serialises exactly as there. `layout_windows: null` is read as absent on both sides and never written; `[]` is invalid.",
